[5] static limit and moving sources
    G(w=0,k) = 1/k^2 exactly for every gamma (friction term ~ w): Newtonian static limit unchanged [exact]
    1 AU, w=370 km/s: IF friction acted on the scalar potential, frame-dipole correction gamma w r/(2c^2) = 6.8e-19 (gamma=H0)
    binary-pulsar orbit 1e9 m: IF friction acted on the scalar potential, frame-dipole correction gamma w r/(2c^2) = 4.5e-21 (gamma=H0)
    Galaxy 10 kpc, 300 km/s: IF friction acted on the scalar potential, frame-dipole correction gamma w r/(2c^2) = 1.1e-09 (gamma=H0)
    TT-only friction (E2 as specified): moving-source TT field is O(w^2/c^2) = 1.5e-06 of U; friction alters it by gamma w r/c^2:
      effective PPN-type term at 1 AU ~ 2.1e-24 U  vs alpha_2-type bound 1.6e-9 x (w/c)^2 = 2.4e-15 U
    scalar-sector friction would give self-drag rate (2 gamma |U|/3Mc^2) for Sun: 1.9e-24 s^-1 (dv/v over t_H = 8.1e-07); TT-only: O((w/c)^4) smaller
    scalar-sector friction would give self-drag rate (2 gamma |U|/3Mc^2) for neutron star: 2.2e-19 s^-1 (dv/v over t_H = 9.6e-02); TT-only: O((w/c)^4) smaller

