    Z=0.05: fitted energy decay rate of the mode = 0.0500 (Ohmic prediction g = Z/m = 0.0500); mode energy lost 0.4684 vs work delivered into the string 0.4684 (mismatch 1.7e-04); string-energy estimator 0.4681
    Z=0.1: fitted energy decay rate of the mode = 0.1002 (Ohmic prediction g = Z/m = 0.1000); mode energy lost 0.4983 vs work delivered into the string 0.4987 (mismatch 9.3e-04); string-energy estimator 0.4982

[9] sink and cosmology
    Hawking viscous fluid with gamma = 1.0 H0: eta = gamma c^2/(16 pi G) = 5.89e+07 Pa s; kinetic estimate eta ~ rho c l/3 with rho <= rho_crit -> l_mfp >= 6.9e+25 m = 2249 Mpc (>> lambda_GW ~ 3e6 m at 100 Hz and >> ell: hydrodynamic damping not available)
    Hawking viscous fluid with gamma = 3.0 H0: eta = gamma c^2/(16 pi G) = 1.77e+08 Pa s; kinetic estimate eta ~ rho c l/3 with rho <= rho_crit -> l_mfp >= 2.1e+26 m = 6746 Mpc (>> lambda_GW ~ 3e6 m at 100 Hz and >> ell: hydrodynamic damping not available)
    Ohmic bath (oscillators at rest in the frame, no gradient energy) -> pressureless sink: rho_s' + 3H rho_s = gamma rho_GW -> steady rho_s = (gamma/3H) rho_GW
    ell=1e-08 m: L_g = ln(2w/H0) = 79.3; rho_GW(eps=1) = 8.08e+06 J/m^3 = 1.5e+16 rho_L; (GW+sink) < rho_L needs eps < 4.9e-17
    ell=2e-07 m: L_g = ln(2w/H0) = 76.3; rho_GW(eps=1) = 4.86e+01 J/m^3 = 9.2e+10 rho_L; (GW+sink) < rho_L needs eps < 8.1e-12
    ell=1e-06 m: L_g = ln(2w/H0) = 74.7; rho_GW(eps=1) = 7.62e-02 J/m^3 = 1.4e+08 rho_L; (GW+sink) < rho_L needs eps < 5.2e-09
    ell=5e-06 m: L_g = ln(2w/H0) = 73.1; rho_GW(eps=1) = 1.19e-04 J/m^3 = 2.3e+05 rho_L; (GW+sink) < rho_L needs eps < 3.3e-06
